    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449-a2">

                <pb facs="0803" n="707" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg707"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 116.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Turner to Mr.
                            Moore.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the Unites States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 25,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your
                    announcement of the intention of his excellency the President to receive Walter
                    Brohm, esq., as consul for the German Empire, on Thursday, the 26th instant, at
                    1 o’clock, together with your solicitation for my attendance on that occasion.
                    Thanking you in advance, Mr. Secretary, for the pleasure I anticipate at being
                    present on so distinguished an occasion,</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. MILTON TURNER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
